b-ac4b-050bce56591a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42853" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=sec⁡x?$\n\n- $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain.\n- $x=\\pi $ is a root. $$\n- $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ is not in the range of the function." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934039/assets/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ thus it is not defined for $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has no zeros.\n\n- Statement III is true. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ does not belong to the range." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42886/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "d7802cb8-4a20-52c0-8156-5490f724fd16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42886/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "69c34c48-163f-55af-a70c-9fdbc06247aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42886/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "29b4e736-1ccc-5b2b-9d84-cb4df6e90942" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42886/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a