6\\pi )?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=sec⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡x=sec⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-8$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sec⁡x=sec⁡(x+2\\cdot (-8)\\cdot \\pi )=sec⁡(x-16\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $sec⁡x=\\sqrt{7},$ then $sec⁡(x-16\\pi )=\\sqrt{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103692/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce45704e-ecea-5c67-bb40-a413f8a0d72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103692"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103701/selection/83b59e0e68f5672a365ced7116e131ac43df92e4e9a53ddf1ed4bc3a0055ed95" :answer/id #uuid "95c5c9b0-0419-5aa4-80ca-2c01f8aa2bdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi -\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103701/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer/id #uuid "0dfd00e9-38f2-50ae-ba29-d9e6169ae111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103701/selection/d5d1180dc785a92aec98c7de73ebd5417615ba14b08a23264349fc417b0ac904" :answer/id #uuid "03d0f9da-3ee2-5c30-92fa-14505ca4ad02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103701/selection/fea7333d69600e2d11fdf823c1e9fccab4ade0493f065251a4fc8f6b617a7578" :answer/id #uuid "e48b367e-ea3b-534f-8139-ccbd17ec8627" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103701/selection/e4feab3a7179f2a87633c6e7922d72261df298535ed5bf9932c62a0940c0196c" :answer/id #uuid "49395bd1-9c98-51b3-b77c-6d10e1c6742a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103701/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e537e696-db4f-5020-ad8d-75cd7f1791db" :answ